From 7298ef69f04650089e2401a5829e170547036afa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Resonate web port <dave.torosyan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 06:00:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Batch robustness: export the sheets that succeeded, fail
 loudly on an unusable music font

A browser user's conversion failed on every sheet at HEADERS with
"IllegalArgumentException: Width (0) and height (0) cannot be <= 0": the
Bravura font was created (family Bravura) but glyph outlines came back
empty, so ShapeSymbol.buildImage allocated a 0x0 image. And since a single
failed sheet fails the whole transcription, nothing was exported.

Partial results, in batch:
- SheetStub remembers the step that failed (getFailedStep; null when the
  failure, Errors included, occurred before any step). Book logs one stable
  line per failed sheet, "Sheet#N failed at STEP: reason" (STEP is "?" when
  unknown; wrapper exceptions skipped; a step timeout reads "timeout after N
  seconds") and discards the sheet: flagged invalid but, unlike a sheet with
  no music, skipped without breaking the score. An Error raised on the
  calling thread, or an OutOfMemoryError anywhere, is reported the same way
  and stops the processing of the other sheets.
- Book.transcribe goes on with the other sheets when every sheet either
  reached the last step or was discarded, logging "Partial transcription:
  K of N sheets, without failed sheets [#..]", followed by "Partial
  transcription: first sheet failed, title/tempo/time signature may be
  missing" when the first sheet is among them (score header data generally
  comes from it). Scores are rebuilt, so the export stays a single movement
  ("exported to <path>.mxl" as before). Discarded sheets are not processed
  again. No export when no sheet succeeded, nor when a music font was found
  unusable (even if only the last sheet failed).
- Book.updateScores links a sheet to its nearest non-discarded neighbors,
  so the sheets after a discarded one see the same preceding page as if
  the discarded sheet were absent from the input.
- Voices.refineScore never connects slurs, ties or voices across a
  discarded sheet (whether it had music or was removed for having none).
- Consequently a sheet without staves no longer prevents the export of the
  other sheets. SheetStub.decideOnRemoval keeps its reason in the exception
  ("Sheet removed: Too few staff filaments: 0 ...").

Music font:
- OmrFont.createFont logs creation failures at WARN with the exception (was
  DEBUG), makes a second attempt, and warns when a platform font replaces a
  custom font. New system property audiveris.fonts.dir: a folder whose font
  files are read in place with Font.createFont(int, File), e.g. "/str" in the
  browser, so that no temporary font copy goes to java.io.tmpdir (IndexedDB
  under CheerpJ). The font cache is a concurrent map (fonts are cached and
  evicted by any processing thread).
- MusicFont checks every font of a new size before use and caching: the
  expected family, then glyphs. The first time for a family, every code
  point its Symbols define (156 for Bravura: clefs incl. small/8va/8vb,
  heads, flags, rests, accidentals, dynamics, time digits...) must map to a
  glyph with a non-empty outline (the bounds symbol layouts use); later
  sizes check the glyphs of key shapes only (clefs, heads, accidentals,
  quarter rest, flag). The key glyphs must also paint pixels in an ARGB
  image, as symbol images are built. Natively the startup check takes 35-55
  ms, a new size 3-4 ms (20-30 ms at 200+ pt), 6 sizes for a 6-page score.
- An unusable font is created again, once per family (and then from the
  application resources, not from audiveris.fonts.dir). If still unusable,
  the family is flagged and MusicFont logs one ERROR line, which is the
  marker of an unusable music font:
    ERROR [] MusicFont ... | Music font Bravura unusable: 1 of 156 glyphs
    have no outline: F_CLEF U+E062 at 64pt (family=Bravura name=Bravura
    glyphs=3693)
  listing the failing glyphs (shape and code point, up to 20 per kind:
  "have no outline", "are missing", "key glyphs paint no pixel"). In batch,
  an UnusableFontException follows; in the GUI the font is used as is.
- MusicFont.checkMusicFont, run at batch start, checks the default family:
  if unusable, Main runs no batch task (exit status 1, no sheet processed).
- In batch, ShapeSymbol.buildImage no longer allocates a 0x0 image: empty
  symbol bounds flag the font as unusable (same ERROR line if first, e.g.
  "Music font Bravura unusable: no outline for F_CLEF U+E062 at 80pt"), and
  so does a symbol image with no pixel when computing a clef centroid; no
  silent default. The sheet is logged "Sheet#N failed at STEP: Music font
  Bravura unusable: ..." and the book stops: no export. In the GUI, a
  warning and no image (or the box center), as before.

No change on healthy input: the MusicXML exported for the four test scores
is byte-identical to the previous build.

